From: Dimitri John Ledkov <dimitri.ledkov@surgut.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2025 00:46:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] entitlements: Grant entitlements for bc-fips 2.1 compat

Runtime.addShutdownHook is always forbidden, but new versions of
bc-fips and bc-rng-jent require it. There is no policy entitlement to
allow it, thus lift the forbidden policy.

bc-fips 2.1.0 has native libraries capability, thus grant loading
native libraries.

bc.rng.jent also uses native libraries, thus grant loading native
libraries to that scope.

Unconditionally grant these entitlements to allow running with bc-fips
in unapproved mode.

Note that the entitlements code is broken, because it does not correctly query security property of bouncycastle.
---
 .../entitlement/bridge/EntitlementChecker.java    |  2 --
 .../entitlement/qa/test/SystemActions.java        |  5 -----
 .../bootstrap/HardcodedEntitlements.java          | 15 +++++++++++----
 .../policy/ElasticsearchEntitlementChecker.java   |  5 -----
 4 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

